				{
					bark("Surely you have heard of the Tempest? Oh, I see, we are just a visitor to this city, eh? Well, the Tempest is the handmaiden to the Great Titan of Water Hydros. ");
					askList -= <<"What is a Tempest? ">>;
					askList += <<"What are the Tempest duties? ", "Who is Hydros? ">>;
				}
				case "What are the Tempest duties? "
				{
					bark("How is it we don't know about the Tempest? Are we a very busy person or perhaps a little simple-minded? Well, no matter. The Tempest has the ability to touch a portion of the power of Hydros. ");
					askList -= <<"What are the Tempest duties? ">>;
				}
				case "Who is Hydros? "
				{
					bark("Ah, the great Water Titan, the Lurker. What ever title she goes by, she is the most powerful of the Titans. The Lady Mordea can use a bit of Hydro's power to control the weather and all things of water. ");
					askList -= <<"Who is Hydros? ">>;
				}
				case "Tell me about Lady Mordea. "
				{
					bark("She is a wise ruler and a fierce leader, most worthy of the title, 'Tempest'. So many times people say 'This thing or that thing cannot be done.' and yet she does it. Do we not now have much lower crime than under the previous Tempest? There is your proof! ");
					askList -= <<"Tell me about Lady Mordea. ">>;
					askList += <<"Tell me about the title 'Tempest'. ">>;
				}
				case "Tell me about the title 'Tempest'. "
				{
					bark("My, my, my. We really are a bit simple, aren't we? Perhaps we've been drinking a bit too much of Orlok's ale, hmmmm? Well, just to humor you, I'll refresh your memory. The title of Tempest is given to the leader of the city of Tenebrae. To become the Tempest, one must have been born of the royal family. It is only through heredity one may sit upon the throne. ");
					askList -= <<"Tell me about the title 'Tempest'. ">>;
					askList += <<"Why is the Tempestry hereditary? ">>;
				}
				case "Why is the Tempestry hereditary? "
				{
					bark("Because the powers that are necessary to bear the title are only transferred from parent to child. Lady Mordea received the power from her father. Does that make things a little clearer for you? ");
					askList -= <<"Why is the Tempestry hereditary? ">>;
					askList += <<"Who was Lady Mordea's father? ">>;
				}
				case "Who was Lady Mordea's father? "
				{
					bark("Didn't you learn anything as a child? Lord Keldan was Lady Mordea's father! And might I add that Lady Mordea is twice the Tempest Lord Keldan ever was. Why, if it weren't for his wife's encouragement, he would never have admitted his powers and assumed the title of Tempest, and then where would we be? ");
					askList -= <<"Who was Lady Mordea's father? ">>;
				}
				case "What more important things? "
				{
					bark("Well, if it were to be common knowledge what the Tempest does, then there would be no mystery...no majestic mystique, hmmm? ");
					askList -= <<"What more important things? ">>;
				}
				case "What do you know about Bentic? "
				{
					bark("That knave! He was conducting forbidden research. Why I am pleased we took care of him when we did. Nipped that problem right in the bud, we did. ");
					askList -= <<"What do you know about Bentic? ">>;
					askList = <<"You 'took care of him?' ", "What is 'forbidden research'? ">>;
				}
				case "You 'took care of him?' "
				{
					bark("He was executed, of course. ");
					askList -= <<"You 'took care of him?' ">>;
					askList = <<"Executed?! ">>;
				}
				case "Executed?! "
				{
					bark("Yes, on the docks. Oh, it is the best way. And we do it on the docks so that the site is easily washed down. No mess, no fuss. It is my job to schedule the executions. I keep records of all executions in my log book. ");
					askList -= <<"Executed?! ">>;
					askList += <<"What do you mean the 'best way'? ", "What log book? ">>;
				}
				case "What log book? "
				{
					bark("Why, my log book. I have to keep records of these sorts of things, you know. Why, how else would we keep track of expenses and such? Lady Mordea requires a full accounting of these things. It's all part of the thankless job of the seneschal. But that's all right, just knowing that I've done my job to the best of my ability is all the reward I need. ");
					askList -= <<"What log book? ">>;
				}
				case "What do you mean the 'best way'? "
				{
					bark("The quicker the better. Can't have prisoners cluttering up the jails, costing the taxpayers' money. This way we keep costs down and add a serious deterrent to those who might be thinking of breaking the law. ");
					askList -= <<"What do you mean the 'best way'? ">>;
				}
				case "What is 'forbidden research'? "
				{
					bark("If I told you what research was forbidden, then I'd just be encouraging you, wouldn't I, hmmmm? ");
					askList -= <<"What is 'forbidden research'? ">>;
				}
				case "What do you know about Devon? "
				{
					bark("That trouble maker. Well, he will be taken care of, and well he deserves it. ");
					askList -= <<"What do you know about Devon? ">>;
					askList += <<"What are the charges? ">>;
				}
				case "What are the charges? "
				{
					bark("That is privileged information. It will be revealed at the execution. Good heavens, it's almost time. Oh, and there is -so- much to do before an execution. Arrange for the clean up crew, make sure Shaana's axe is sharpened...I've enjoyed our little talk, but I must leave now. Good day. ");
					exitConvo();
					return;
				}
				case "I would like to speak with you. "
				{
					bark("Well, have we learned our manners? ");
					askList = <<"yes, sir ", "no ">>;
				}
				case "yes, sir "
				{
					bark("Well, that's a little more like it. Perhaps there is some hope for us after all, hmmmm? Now, what can I do for you? ");
					salkindPissed = 0;
					askList -= <<"yes, sir ", "no ">>;
					askList += <<"What do you do? ">>;
				}
